  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P({a,{a,b}})={\u2205,{a},{{a,b}},{a,{a,b}}}$\n- $P({a,{b}})={\u2205,{a},{{a,b}}}$\n- $P({{\u2205}})={\u2205,{{\u2205}}}$",
  "worked_solution": "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $\u2205.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the power set of the set ${a,{a,b}}$ is ${\u2205,{a},{{a,b}},{a,{a,b}}}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that we are given the set ${a,{b}}.$ So, its power set must be ${\u2205,{a},{{b}},{a,{b}}}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the power set of the set ${{\u2205}}$ is ${\u2205,{{\u2205}}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
